1
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,920
Try stepping away and take a look.

2
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:28,600
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling.

3
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:35,300
Walking while looking back,
hand in hand with Mom.

4
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:42,440
Hey, that strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:47,700
So, the tiles of the shopping arcade...

6
00:00:48,260 --> 00:00:53,480
I tried walking only on the black ones.

7
00:00:56,240 --> 00:01:01,780
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten.

8
00:01:02,740 --> 00:01:09,080
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

9
00:01:09,590 --> 00:01:14,660
Go on, turn that corner.

10
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:19,900
You can meet everyone, everyone.

11
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:27,800
There's Kameari surely Kameari is there.

12
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:33,060
Everyone, come on over to our town!

13
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:34,580
Thank you.

14
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:43,240
Another politician's corruption scandal

15
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:46,600
They only ever care about
lining their own pockets.

16
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:49,760
They don't think about the public at all.

17
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:52,400
Unless we fix Japan's broken system,

18
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:54,280
I don't think corruption
will ever disappear.

19
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:56,140
What are you talking about?

20
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:02,340
Is that so?
Then it has nothing to do with me.

21
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:05,000
Nyahehehehe.

22
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,760
As usual,
you couldn't care less about politics.

23
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:11,200
Life's easier when you don't
know anything about the world.

24
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:15,360
As long as you can build model kits and read manga every day,
you're happy, right?

25
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:17,720
I envy idiots like that.

26
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:20,860
What a thing to say!

27
00:02:20,860 --> 00:02:25,580
That makes it sound like I go through life
without thinking about anything at all!

28
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:26,880
Am I wrong?

29
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:30,120
I think about politics in my own way, too.

30
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:34,280
Well then, name five politicians.

31
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:36,620
What's wrong, don't you know?

32
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:38,080
First of all...

33
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:41,461
First, Ryūnosuke Akutagawa,

34
00:02:41,511 --> 00:02:43,417
Hikoroku Hayashiya,

35
00:02:43,467 --> 00:02:45,726
Mikimatsu Yanagiya,

36
00:02:45,776 --> 00:02:48,036
Pāko Hayashiya,

37
00:02:48,086 --> 00:02:50,780
Kairakutei Black

38
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:52,960
Not one of you got a single right answer,
did you?

39
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:56,740
Well, you'd be better off
dying without ever knowing.

40
00:02:57,580 --> 00:03:00,880
There's no need to say it so dismissively,
is there?

41
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:06,340
Trying to teach you politics is harder
than teaching English to a chimpanzee.

42
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:09,200
Even if they didn't do it,

43
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:10,620
whether it's true or not,

44
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:15,520
but dismissing something right away just
because you don't understand it isn't good, is it?

45
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:20,120
Why don't you teach Ryo-chan clearly and carefully,
so he can understand?

46
00:03:20,580 --> 00:03:20,980
I see.

47
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:25,640
All right, then, so you can understand too, let me explain about
"o-shoku."

48
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:30,340
I'll explain it to you
very gently and carefully.

49
00:03:30,340 --> 00:03:32,420
Let's say there's an animal village here.

50
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:35,400
We are residents of the animal village.

51
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:39,120
Our village has decided to build a building.

52
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:43,640
So we're going to choose a
company to do the construction work,

53
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:45,700
Those who want to build, raise your hands.

54
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:50,720
But in reality, the construction
company has already been chosen.

55
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:55,500
A lot of money flows to the village
chief and the politicians on the board.

56
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:59,800
And since the building is going
to be paid for with taxes anyway,

57
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:03,000
they set a budget several
times the real cost.

58
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:08,980
Then they split up that inflated money and profit behind the scenes.
That's how it works.

59
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:12,660
Once the construction is over,
the under-the-table money stops coming in,

60
00:04:12,660 --> 00:04:15,460
so they press the village chief
to approve the next project.

61
00:04:15,460 --> 00:04:17,480
Of course, they hand over bribes too.

62
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:19,640
"Please take good care of us, oink!"

63
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:24,280
Since the village chief profits too, he gives the
go-ahead to build as many buildings as they like.

64
00:04:24,280 --> 00:04:25,760
Okay, all set.

65
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:34,460
Put simply, this is how it works.

66
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:35,420
Got it?

67
00:04:35,420 --> 00:04:37,800
Our taxes, being used like that -

68
00:04:38,340 --> 00:04:41,800
hundreds of billions a year go into public works projects,
you know.

69
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:42,520
What?

70
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:44,760
Hundreds of billions, I tell you!

71
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:46,020
Seriously, that's true.

72
00:04:46,020 --> 00:04:49,160
Is it really, really,
really being spent that much?

73
00:04:51,260 --> 00:04:52,220
This is terrible!

74
00:04:52,220 --> 00:04:54,060
We've got to tell everyone right away!

75
00:04:56,260 --> 00:04:58,260
Only Ryo-chan doesn't know, you know.

76
00:04:58,980 --> 00:05:00,840
Why don't the citizens get angry?

77
00:05:00,840 --> 00:05:03,860
If they do that to you,
you've got to complain, damn it!

78
00:05:03,860 --> 00:05:07,700
Even when money moves out of sight,
people just don't feel it.

79
00:05:07,700 --> 00:05:09,920
We've half given up on it.

80
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:14,080
Not complaining is the same as saying yes,
you know.

81
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:16,540
The money we sweat blood working for...

82
00:05:16,540 --> 00:05:19,480
There are guys who stash it all away and rake in the cash,
you know.

83
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:24,580
I don't think being taken
for fools is anything new.

84
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:26,980
Isn't there an election coming up, though?

85
00:05:27,260 --> 00:05:27,980
Election?

86
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:32,100
I see, an election

87
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:33,220
That's right.

88
00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:36,200
In an election, you vote for
someone you think is trustworthy,

89
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:39,500
and have that person work in your place.

90
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:42,480
If that person takes action,
will corruption disappear?

91
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:45,180
It may not be that simple, though.

92
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:46,300
See? I told you!

93
00:05:46,580 --> 00:05:49,500
Anyway,
who can really know who's trustworthy...

94
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:51,420
Can anyone really tell so easily?

95
00:05:52,340 --> 00:05:53,840
W-well, that's true...

96
00:05:55,780 --> 00:05:57,360
I'll run in the election myself.

97
00:05:57,360 --> 00:06:00,500
Leaving it to others isn't my style.

98
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:03,520
If I become a politician,
everything will be solved.

99
00:06:03,520 --> 00:06:07,020
That's a whole different thing from running for class representative,
you know.

100
00:06:07,020 --> 00:06:10,840
Yes, elections need a lot of campaign funds.

101
00:06:11,460 --> 00:06:13,460
So, Reiko Akimoto.

102
00:06:13,460 --> 00:06:16,320
Could you lend me a little money?

103
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:17,620
I thought as much.

104
00:06:18,180 --> 00:06:19,240
I'm not interested.

105
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:22,660
Why should I have to go along
with such a ridiculous thing?

106
00:06:22,660 --> 00:06:24,140
What do you mean, ridiculous?

107
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:27,860
Fine, I won't ask you! Hey, Nakagawa.

108
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:29,980
I'm refusing too.

109
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:31,360
W-why?

110
00:06:31,540 --> 00:06:33,934
The Nakagawa Group doesn't give money

111
00:06:33,984 --> 00:06:36,080
to any party or any candidate.
That's our motto.

112
00:06:37,260 --> 00:06:38,960
What, there's no way at all?

113
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:40,560
There's absolutely no way.

114
00:06:40,740 --> 00:06:42,360
Absolutely, positively no?

115
00:06:42,520 --> 00:06:43,920
Absolutely, positively no.

116
00:06:44,220 --> 00:06:46,120
Even though I'm begging like this, still no?

117
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:48,240
No matter how much you beg, it's still no.

118
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:52,460
Seriously! Fine, I'll handle it myself!

119
00:06:57,240 --> 00:06:59,640
Is Ryo-chan really
planning to run for office?

120
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:01,640
What a simple-minded guy.

121
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:04,820
But if he actually gets elected,

122
00:07:04,820 --> 00:07:08,060
I'm worried it'll change
the direction of Japan.

123
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:10,240
Yes!

124
00:07:11,340 --> 00:07:11,980
Got it!

125
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:19,380
Sorry to keep you waiting.

126
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:21,420
You're certainly quick.

127
00:07:21,420 --> 00:07:23,600
I'm Ryotsu!

128
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:27,440
If you're running for election,
leave it to me.

129
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:32,160
Sure-Win Election Contractor,
Daigorō Shūgiin!

130
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:36,160
Yes, from small village mayoral races all
the way to the US presidential election.

131
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:41,960
In every kind of election, the candidates I've
served as campaign strategist have always won.

132
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:45,580
Sensei, leave it to me.

133
00:07:45,580 --> 00:07:48,780
I'll make sure you walk the red carpet.

134
00:07:48,780 --> 00:07:51,800
Sen-sensei... what a lovely ring that has.

135
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:55,680
You'll really get me elected, right?

136
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:56,980
Of course.

137
00:07:57,940 --> 00:07:59,600
Alright, I'll leave it to you.

138
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:00,900
Yes, thank you very much.

139
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:05,400
Then I'd like to discuss the
campaign strategy right away.

140
00:08:06,240 --> 00:08:07,880
Then, this way to the car.

141
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:14,040
By the way, Sensei,
how much will the election package cost?

142
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:15,200
I don't have that kind of money.

143
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:17,580
Not a single yen?

144
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:18,280
Yeah.

145
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:19,880
So it's no good?

146
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:22,080
If you can't say, that's fine.

147
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:25,160
Let's start by raising the funds.

148
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:26,140
How?

149
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:29,520
The quickest way is probably a party.

150
00:08:30,580 --> 00:08:33,260
Shall we rally behind Officer Ryotsu, then?

151
00:08:35,020 --> 00:08:36,920
The guest list is pretty impressive,
isn't it?

152
00:08:37,660 --> 00:08:39,920
The Rolling Stones and Mōmusu, no less.

153
00:08:39,920 --> 00:08:42,620
Ryōtarō Sugi and Norika Fujiwara, too.

154
00:08:43,140 --> 00:08:44,540
I wonder if this is really true.

155
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:45,840
I don't know.

156
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:48,300
Ken's supposedly selling like crazy, though.

157
00:08:48,300 --> 00:08:51,220
Anyway,
let's definitely go and check it out.

158
00:09:04,040 --> 00:09:06,440
Summers these days really are too scary,
aren't they?

159
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:09,380
I just can't resist that sidelong glance!

160
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:11,740
When did they even come to Japan?

161
00:09:13,140 --> 00:09:14,320
It's really packed, isn't it?

162
00:09:14,860 --> 00:09:17,320
Is it really okay to
gather this many people?

163
00:09:17,860 --> 00:09:20,820
But the fans are all mixed together,
it's a total mess.

164
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:24,720
Today, despite your busy schedules,

165
00:09:24,720 --> 00:09:28,800
thank you for gathering in such large
numbers for Kankichi Ryotsu-sensei.

166
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:30,480
We truly thank you.

167
00:09:31,580 --> 00:09:33,920
please enjoy the delicious food as you dine,

168
00:09:33,920 --> 00:09:36,240
and have the most wonderful time.

169
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:47,720
Aren't you cute

170
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:50,640
Don't go canoodling with a bum like this!

171
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:52,920
Hey, what's that supposed to mean!

172
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:55,160
Aaaaaaaah!

173
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:57,580
Why, you - !

174
00:09:57,960 --> 00:10:02,340
Drunk and ganging up on a young lady like that,
that's no way to treat a lady, you know.

175
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,320
What! Sanpin's getting cocky!

176
00:10:05,660 --> 00:10:07,060
You're just an egg! Let's go, come on!

177
00:10:07,280 --> 00:10:07,600
Hup!

178
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:08,620
Yaah!

179
00:10:10,780 --> 00:10:17,600
On your father's life,

180
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:24,680
on the thread of Misujin,

181
00:10:26,420 --> 00:10:29,220
I stake

182
00:10:29,800 --> 00:10:33,000
three of them

183
00:10:34,260 --> 00:10:39,180
Love's Ometsuzure

184
00:10:42,860 --> 00:10:44,660
Thank you so much for saving us
from that dangerous situation.

185
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:47,900
Please, do come by our home.

186
00:10:47,900 --> 00:10:49,340
Let us at least offer
you something as thanks.

187
00:10:49,340 --> 00:10:51,160
It was nothing really.

188
00:10:51,160 --> 00:10:53,000
Well, never mind that. Your daughter...

189
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:55,080
I'm really glad she wasn't hurt.

190
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:56,640
Well then, excuse me.

191
00:10:57,620 --> 00:10:58,960
Hey there, traveler.

192
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:00,900
Miss...

193
00:11:00,900 --> 00:11:03,320
I'm just a lowly wandering crow,
as they say.

194
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:06,320
Such a sorry state of affairs. My heart's obligations are worth more than gold,
you see.

195
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:09,180
Well then,
do take care and live well, won't you.

196
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:14,740
What on earth is this?

197
00:11:19,380 --> 00:11:20,620
Thank you for watching.

198
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:23,700
And now, let me introduce the performers.

199
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:27,520
First, special guest Ryotaro Sugi.

200
00:11:28,540 --> 00:11:30,480
S-Sugi Ryotaro!

201
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:33,340
It's not Ryotaro Sugi, it's Sumo!

202
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:35,860
Next, Norika Fujiwara.

203
00:11:36,920 --> 00:11:40,440
Whoa! Eek!
That's nothing like Norika Fujiwara!

204
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:44,100
This girl is definitely Norika Fujiwara.

205
00:11:44,460 --> 00:11:47,300
Sir, take a good look at the pamphlet.

206
00:11:47,620 --> 00:11:48,000
Whoa!

207
00:11:48,660 --> 00:11:49,140
Aaah!

208
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:52,700
Aaah! She's not Norika Fujiwara!

209
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:54,900
It's not a cajón, it's a quill!

210
00:11:55,940 --> 00:11:57,660
Aaah! Aaah! Aaah! Aaah!

211
00:11:57,660 --> 00:11:59,800
This is fraud! Aaah! Aaah! Aaah!

212
00:12:00,900 --> 00:12:02,260
Using such underhanded tricks!

213
00:12:02,780 --> 00:12:05,720
It's exactly as the pamphlet said,
so there's nothing we can do.

214
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:09,800
At this rate,
the Rolling Stones and Morning Musume too

215
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:15,620
Thank you for waiting.

216
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:19,160
And now,
the second half of our music show begins!

217
00:12:19,680 --> 00:12:21,500
Performing for you tonight,
the ever-familiar

218
00:12:23,020 --> 00:12:25,380
Rolling Stones!

219
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:32,080
And the backup dancers are

220
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:35,380
No Musume

221
00:12:39,780 --> 00:12:40,680
Just as I thought.

222
00:12:40,680 --> 00:12:43,560
It's so ridiculous I can't even be angry.

223
00:12:43,560 --> 00:12:45,540
Now, let's have you listen to this.

224
00:12:46,180 --> 00:12:47,520
"My Way"

225
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:50,600
Now.

226
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:51,160
Already.

227
00:12:54,620 --> 00:12:57,180
I don't want to get involved,
so let's hurry up and go home.

228
00:12:57,580 --> 00:12:57,980
Yeah, that's right.

229
00:12:58,460 --> 00:13:00,040
Well, it's about what I expected.

230
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:02,280
I went through such a rough time.

231
00:13:02,780 --> 00:13:06,740
But Sensei,
we've got the campaign funds all set now.

232
00:13:06,740 --> 00:13:07,680
I see.

233
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:10,140
You're really going to run in the
election even after going through this?

234
00:13:10,140 --> 00:13:12,820
I'm absolutely, positively going to win!

235
00:13:24,620 --> 00:13:26,440
Good morning, sir.

236
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:29,720
What do you think, sir? Of this office?

237
00:13:29,720 --> 00:13:31,700
Well, it's okay, I suppose.

238
00:13:36,940 --> 00:13:38,880
What is this poster?

239
00:13:38,880 --> 00:13:41,700
I don't remember taking a picture like this!

240
00:13:41,700 --> 00:13:44,120
And why am I dressed as a rugby player?

241
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:47,400
It's an image strategy to win votes.

242
00:13:47,820 --> 00:13:51,920
Ordinary people are easily taken
in by a fresh image like this.

243
00:13:52,420 --> 00:13:55,680
That's why we used a computer
to composite the photo.

244
00:13:56,140 --> 00:13:59,560
By the way, I also changed the name
to hiragana so it's easier to remember.

245
00:14:01,060 --> 00:14:03,220
Who bought this daruma?!

246
00:14:03,920 --> 00:14:05,560
Yes! That would be me!

247
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:09,120
Ryotsu-sensei is a big-scale candidate!

248
00:14:09,420 --> 00:14:11,220
You made the teacher look bad!

249
00:14:11,420 --> 00:14:13,280
I'm so sorry!

250
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:16,380
After all, it has to be this big,

251
00:14:17,420 --> 00:14:19,640
Sensei, you're going on a
campaign speaking tour now.

252
00:14:19,640 --> 00:14:20,500
A campaign speaking tour?

253
00:14:21,620 --> 00:14:24,620
You mean the "once I'm elected" thing?

254
00:14:24,620 --> 00:14:25,580
That's right.

255
00:14:25,980 --> 00:14:29,340
But campaign promises like
that don't matter at all.

256
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:33,780
After all, hardly anyone who
gets elected keeps their promises.

257
00:14:34,220 --> 00:14:37,120
So you just need to win over the hearts
of the people listening right there,

258
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:40,440
with a speech that hits them with an
impact that grabs them by the throat.

259
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:44,520
I'm on the side of all the
salarymen and office ladies.

260
00:14:45,540 --> 00:14:47,520
The Japanese work far too much.

261
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:50,660
Once I'm elected, four-day weekends,

262
00:14:50,660 --> 00:14:53,180
three hours of work a day,

263
00:14:53,180 --> 00:14:54,700
and two months of vacation.

264
00:14:54,700 --> 00:14:57,540
I will absolutely make this happen.

265
00:14:59,040 --> 00:15:01,420
For young people, CG is 10,100 yen.

266
00:15:01,420 --> 00:15:03,120
Video software is 150 yen.

267
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:04,980
Movie tickets are 80 yen.

268
00:15:04,980 --> 00:15:07,240
Also, a children's
two-wheeler-only licensing system.

269
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:09,040
A four-day school week.

270
00:15:09,040 --> 00:15:10,620
I will keep all of these promises.

271
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:16,520
To all the housewives, if I'm elected, I'll
adopt a nationwide public meal system...

272
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:19,640
I'll abolish all home cooking.
Just you watch.

273
00:15:21,560 --> 00:15:22,980
Thank you for your hard work, sensei.

274
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:25,860
We've got a packed schedule after this, too.

275
00:15:26,400 --> 00:15:28,060
Please rest for about 20 minutes.

276
00:15:28,060 --> 00:15:30,540
But we can't just sleep
while waving our hands.

277
00:15:30,540 --> 00:15:33,820
We're showing this outside the car,
so don't worry.

278
00:15:33,820 --> 00:15:35,560
Well, you're clearly not cut out for this.

279
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:38,420
We're back.

280
00:15:38,420 --> 00:15:39,280
Camera, hurry up!

281
00:15:40,620 --> 00:15:41,740
Just as we planned.

282
00:15:41,740 --> 00:15:43,980
Leave it to me.
I'm confident in my acting skills.

283
00:15:49,380 --> 00:15:51,420
Hello everyone.

284
00:15:51,420 --> 00:15:53,380
Ryo-san, how's it going?
Are you getting any response?

285
00:15:53,380 --> 00:15:54,760
Can't make out a single thing.

286
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:57,200
I'm just doing my best.

287
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:59,840
Look at all that sweat!
Wow, you're really working hard.

288
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:01,480
Sensei, your meal is ready.

289
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:03,380
Thanks for your hard work.

290
00:16:06,260 --> 00:16:07,860
Just rice balls?

291
00:16:07,860 --> 00:16:09,900
How do you keep your strength up on that?

292
00:16:10,620 --> 00:16:13,060
If you died during a campaign as a politician,
that would be your dream, right?

293
00:16:13,060 --> 00:16:14,280
Wonderful.

294
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:17,200
Sensei, there's a telegram from your family.

295
00:16:26,240 --> 00:16:27,380
What's wrong?

296
00:16:27,380 --> 00:16:30,020
My father... my father has passed away.

297
00:16:31,080 --> 00:16:34,940
He fought his illness relying
only on my election victory.

298
00:16:36,260 --> 00:16:37,240
It's a shame.

299
00:16:38,180 --> 00:16:40,580
You must win the election
for my late father's sake.

300
00:16:40,580 --> 00:16:43,500
I'd like to offer my respects at the altar.

301
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:47,340
This brings in 30,000
yen in condolence money.

302
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:48,940
But is that really all right?

303
00:16:49,420 --> 00:16:51,500
I went ahead and killed
your father without asking.

304
00:16:51,500 --> 00:16:53,540
Don't worry about that.

305
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:58,200
Your father has been invited to
a hot spring far away from town.

306
00:16:58,200 --> 00:17:01,360
I've made sure he stays put
until the election is over.

307
00:17:02,280 --> 00:17:03,080
Thank you very much, Sensei.

308
00:17:03,760 --> 00:17:05,040
Not at all.

309
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:07,520
So they've finally gone.

310
00:17:08,700 --> 00:17:09,460
I'm starving.

311
00:17:10,780 --> 00:17:12,220
So how's the vote count looking?

312
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:13,720
Well, let's see.

313
00:17:14,460 --> 00:17:16,200
We're doing well in the old downtown areas,

314
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:17,680
but we still don't have enough votes.

315
00:17:18,180 --> 00:17:20,720
If we could get another 100,000 votes,
we'd be safe.

316
00:17:20,720 --> 00:17:22,740
Leave it to me, I've got a good idea.

317
00:17:23,380 --> 00:17:24,160
Chief.

318
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:26,500
Ryo-chan,
your campaign broadcast is about to start.

319
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:28,400
That guy appearing on TV for something

320
00:17:28,400 --> 00:17:30,000
other than a case?
I never thought I'd see it.

321
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:32,220
Next, the independent

322
00:17:32,220 --> 00:17:34,020
candidate Kankichi
Ryotsu's campaign broadcast

323
00:17:34,020 --> 00:17:34,660
will now be presented.

324
00:17:35,920 --> 00:17:38,360
Born in Asakusa,
graduated from a vocational high school.

325
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:40,180
Police detention record: 15 times.

326
00:17:40,180 --> 00:17:41,920
Thanks to that connection,
became a police officer.

327
00:17:41,920 --> 00:17:43,220
Countless letters of reprimand.

328
00:17:43,220 --> 00:17:45,160
Disciplinary actions: 18 times.

329
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:47,500
It's like he's putting his shame on display.

330
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:53,080
Isn't it meaningless?

331
00:17:53,080 --> 00:17:55,240
It's pointless, isn't it?

332
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:58,860
Ladies and gentlemen, it's meaningless.
Welcome to today's gathering.

333
00:18:00,260 --> 00:18:01,600
Now, the postcards.

334
00:18:01,600 --> 00:18:04,300
From Katsushika Ward,
from Mr. Kankichi Ryotsu.

335
00:18:05,040 --> 00:18:06,680
I wonder if it has any meaning or not.

336
00:18:06,680 --> 00:18:08,980
The Chief says to me,

337
00:18:08,980 --> 00:18:11,760
"Try to act a little more decently,"
that line.

338
00:18:11,760 --> 00:18:12,800
Ready... go!

339
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:14,800
It's pointless, isn't it?

340
00:18:15,580 --> 00:18:16,960
What is this?

341
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:20,120
Looks like they mistook
it for a variety show.

342
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:22,180
I expected as much, but

343
00:18:23,020 --> 00:18:24,160
around here,

344
00:18:24,160 --> 00:18:25,360
to everyone

345
00:18:25,360 --> 00:18:27,340
you'll be taking me, you know.

346
00:18:27,340 --> 00:18:28,760
In tomorrow's vote,

347
00:18:28,760 --> 00:18:31,840
please be sure to write "Tanuki Saburo."

348
00:18:31,840 --> 00:18:32,700
Please,

349
00:18:32,700 --> 00:18:35,320
make him a man who never sleeps.

350
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:38,360
For housewives' ally Hanamaru Yoshiko,
please give your pure

351
00:18:38,360 --> 00:18:38,820
Pyoo!

352
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:50,700
Sorry for the disturbance, candidates.

353
00:18:50,700 --> 00:18:51,860
Who are you people?

354
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:55,560
We're the Ryotsu Kankichi
Hopeless Support Corps!

355
00:18:55,560 --> 00:18:57,380
First up, Candidate Tanuki.

356
00:18:57,900 --> 00:19:04,420
Lying to your wife about a fact-finding trip and running off to beauty shows and hot springs?
Hopeless!

357
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:07,740
Is that really such a bother?

358
00:19:07,740 --> 00:19:10,180
No, I'm not that sleepy at all.

359
00:19:11,580 --> 00:19:12,700
Candidate Sleepy.

360
00:19:13,240 --> 00:19:16,780
Even though you have a pool-sized bath
made entirely of hinoki cypress at home!

361
00:19:16,780 --> 00:19:22,000
Playing the common man and scrubbing old folks' backs at the public bath?
Hopeless!

362
00:19:22,480 --> 00:19:23,860
How do you know that?

363
00:19:23,860 --> 00:19:24,880
Oh no.

364
00:19:27,560 --> 00:19:28,720
Candidate Hanamaru.

365
00:19:28,720 --> 00:19:29,940
W-what is it?

366
00:19:30,400 --> 00:19:34,200
Preaching gender equality
while doing nothing yourself,

367
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:38,840
making your wife handle all the dishes,
laundry, and even the kids' school visits,

368
00:19:39,300 --> 00:19:40,700
hopeless!

369
00:19:40,700 --> 00:19:42,480
Well said!

370
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:44,120
That's not unnecessary at all, is it?

371
00:19:46,940 --> 00:19:50,220
Okay, everyone, come on,
say it with me: Kameari's hopeless!

372
00:19:50,220 --> 00:19:52,840
That place is hopeless!

373
00:19:53,660 --> 00:19:55,560
I'm sure it's hopeless.

374
00:19:56,900 --> 00:20:01,020
Everyone's hopeless,
hopeless, hopeless, hopeless!

375
00:20:01,720 --> 00:20:02,120
Thank you.

376
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:06,920
So, in tomorrow's vote, don't you dare
vote for a candidate from outside the city.

377
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:08,700
No, no!

378
00:20:08,700 --> 00:20:09,880
Yesterday's candidate.

379
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:10,980
That's funny!

380
00:20:10,980 --> 00:20:14,520
That chief, this and that.

381
00:20:14,520 --> 00:20:16,840
This won't land, so let's cut it.

382
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:19,860
Stop already, right hand,
left hand, depending on...

383
00:20:19,860 --> 00:20:21,940
Welcome, come on in, come along, right?

384
00:20:22,840 --> 00:20:24,140
Okay, Pop, you're almost done!

385
00:20:24,720 --> 00:20:27,080
What's that, that? Your armpit's that too!

386
00:20:27,740 --> 00:20:28,640
Are you satisfied now?

387
00:20:28,920 --> 00:20:29,320
Yeah.

388
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:30,740
Well then, bye-bye!

389
00:20:34,740 --> 00:20:37,480
No good, no good, it's already an excuse.

390
00:20:37,660 --> 00:20:39,860
Saba-san, if you go out the back,
it's no good!

391
00:20:43,480 --> 00:20:46,450
Now, the vote count began at seven o'clock,

392
00:20:46,500 --> 00:20:48,560
Uda-san, how's it looking over there?

393
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:51,520
Here in Katsushika Ward,
the counting has begun.

394
00:20:52,840 --> 00:20:53,220
Hurry!

395
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:55,640
Sensei, there's no need to rush, it's fine.

396
00:20:56,080 --> 00:20:59,108
Look. According to the
computer's projection,

397
00:20:59,158 --> 00:21:01,160
it shows a 99% chance of winning.

398
00:21:01,700 --> 00:21:02,280
I see.

399
00:21:03,480 --> 00:21:05,740
Looking back, it was a hard fight.

400
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:08,100
Sensei,
the press is eagerly waiting for you.

401
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:10,100
Finally, it's the climax.

402
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:14,320
Sorry to keep you all waiting.

403
00:21:14,980 --> 00:21:17,060
Members of the press, please move closer!

404
00:21:18,180 --> 00:21:20,980
Is this angle okay for
painting in the daruma's eyes?

405
00:21:23,220 --> 00:21:24,840
What do you think, Moriguchi?

406
00:21:24,840 --> 00:21:29,040
I think we can say the public made a wise choice after all,
don't you?

407
00:21:29,040 --> 00:21:31,160
And here's a bulletin just in.

408
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:34,700
It looks like the vote count for
Tokyo's 17th district has finished.

409
00:21:34,700 --> 00:21:35,380
Here it comes!

410
00:21:36,240 --> 00:21:40,180
Candidate Sleepy Kiyoyo,
650,115 votes, elected.

411
00:21:40,780 --> 00:21:44,760
Candidate Hanamaru Yoshiko,
583,585 votes, elected.

412
00:21:44,760 --> 00:21:45,020
What?!

413
00:21:46,020 --> 00:21:51,740
Candidate Tanuki Saburo was considered,
but fell short with 552,113 votes.

414
00:21:52,840 --> 00:21:54,920
Candidate Ryotsu Kankichi
Is that really the number?

415
00:21:55,540 --> 00:21:57,460
Candidate Ryotsu Kankichi, one vote.

416
00:21:57,460 --> 00:21:58,340
One vote!

417
00:21:59,200 --> 00:22:01,780
This TV must be broken, right?!

418
00:22:05,640 --> 00:22:08,620
Excuse me. Candidate Ryotsu has seven votes.

419
00:22:09,860 --> 00:22:11,380
W-what? Seven?

420
00:22:11,500 --> 00:22:14,900
Looks like it's only the number of campaign workers,
this one.

421
00:22:15,880 --> 00:22:18,980
Well, then, Candidate Ryotsu,
who has been the subject of much talk,

422
00:22:18,980 --> 00:22:20,920
seems to have vanished like fireworks.

423
00:22:22,980 --> 00:22:25,880
Politics isn't something to take lightly,
but people like him

424
00:22:26,640 --> 00:22:29,180
Hey, what's going on here?

425
00:22:29,980 --> 00:22:32,880
According to the data,
we were getting plenty of votes.

426
00:22:32,880 --> 00:22:35,080
Then why only seven votes?

427
00:22:36,260 --> 00:22:40,040
It's because the sensei put on
that well-meaning performance.

428
00:22:40,440 --> 00:22:43,620
Even if people like that kind of thing on the spot,
it doesn't translate into votes.

429
00:22:43,980 --> 00:22:45,642
The public is harsh,

430
00:22:45,692 --> 00:22:48,340
so they just don't vote
for people like that.

431
00:22:49,780 --> 00:22:51,600
Everyone, we're done here.

432
00:22:58,780 --> 00:22:59,180
No way...

433
00:23:06,220 --> 00:23:07,340
So that means...

434
00:23:07,340 --> 00:23:10,500
Ryotsu here, I'm ashamed to say,
I've come back.

435
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:13,940
Well, elections are unpredictable, you know.

436
00:23:13,940 --> 00:23:17,820
I was thinking I'd work hard at the
police box again starting tomorrow...

437
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:19,620
What are you talking about?

438
00:23:19,620 --> 00:23:22,260
You're not a police officer anymore,
you know.

439
00:23:23,220 --> 00:23:26,060
When a public servant runs for office,
they lose their job.

440
00:23:26,460 --> 00:23:28,460
It's under Article 90 of
the Public Servants Act.

441
00:23:28,460 --> 00:23:32,540
So in other words, the moment you lost,
you became unemployed.

442
00:23:32,540 --> 00:23:35,140
Didn't you know, senpai?

443
00:23:35,140 --> 00:23:37,740
Poor thing,
things are going to be rough for you now.

444
00:23:37,740 --> 00:23:41,900
Chief, can't you do something about this?

445
00:23:41,900 --> 00:23:46,140
Come on, let go. I can't do anything
about this one with my own power.

446
00:23:46,140 --> 00:23:47,460
How cruel!

447
00:23:47,460 --> 00:23:49,180
Don't come near me, you're annoying.

448
00:23:49,180 --> 00:23:52,000
Chief, please do something!

449
00:23:54,940 --> 00:23:58,260
I hate elections so much!

450
00:24:22,840 --> 00:24:25,820
Your hard work,
your unreasonable demands, all quite right.

451
00:24:26,960 --> 00:24:30,520
Baguette in hand,
looking all poised and composed,

452
00:24:30,520 --> 00:24:33,340
beef bowl, cloudy skies, and extra sauce.

453
00:24:33,340 --> 00:24:36,600
Endless overtime and all that irritation,

454
00:24:37,240 --> 00:24:40,220
ylang-ylang clears it all away,
nice and clean.

455
00:24:43,580 --> 00:24:46,480
Every day is no-problem-brain.

456
00:24:46,480 --> 00:24:50,020
After passing through a hot shower,

457
00:24:50,020 --> 00:24:56,580
every day is no-problem-brain,
revive your energy with a sleep pillow.

458
00:24:59,740 --> 00:25:06,140
Every day is no-problem-brain,
I love little old me like this.

459
00:25:06,140 --> 00:25:12,980
Every day is no-problem-brain,
a Monday with hearts flying all around.

460
00:25:12,980 --> 00:25:17,100
Monday, Monday, no problemain

461
00:25:20,340 --> 00:25:23,620
What? The armored car carrying
the bonuses was attacked!

462
00:25:23,620 --> 00:25:27,020
Damn it, they stole my precious bonus!

463
00:25:27,020 --> 00:25:29,380
I'll get it back no matter what!

464
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:34,000
Plamo and Ozagi,
why are you two making a culprit pun?

465
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:36,680
Next time: Bonus Battle 5

466
00:25:37,220 --> 00:25:38,020
See you then.

467
00:25:38,560 --> 00:25:40,760
Over there is Kameary.

468
00:25:41,840 --> 00:25:44,900
Well, I'm sure it's Kameary.

469
00:25:44,900 --> 00:25:49,120
Everyone, come on over to our town!

470
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:50,680
Thank you.

